                    coach_r3_vppair:        `<strong>Pairing the VP with a quiet expert who holds the veto</strong> turns his energy into a check rather than a takeover, and surfaces a voice that would otherwise vanish. Smart casting.`,
                    coach_r3_vplead:        `<strong>You put the VP in charge.</strong> Energy is not the same as inclusion — he hijacks the discussion and the quiet experts disengage. Contain the loud, surface the quiet.`,
                    coach_r3_open:          `<strong>An open prompt with no forced decision</strong> drifts into discussion, not doing. Kolb's loop never starts without a concrete experience — give them a call they must make.`,
                    coach_r3_lowpressure:   `<strong>No time pressure, no felt decision.</strong> Without a countdown, managers deliberate comfortably and nothing transfers. The pressure is the point.`,
                    coach_r4_whatso:        `<strong>That's the engine.</strong> What happened? → So what? → Now what? converts raw experience into transferable insight. Protect these minutes and the EUR 360,000 is in reach.`,
                    coach_r4_kolb:          `<strong>You closed the loop.</strong> Walking experience → reflect → conceptualise → apply is exactly how doing becomes durable capability. A thrilling exercise without this stops at “experience.”`,
                    coach_r4_recap:         `<strong>A recap is not a debrief.</strong> “Great job — any reflections?” lets most of the learning evaporate. The evidence is unambiguous: structured reflection is where it consolidates.`,
                    coach_r4_nodebrief:     `<strong>You skipped reflection entirely.</strong> You had concrete experience and walked away from it. How much of the EUR 360,000 transfer guarantee did you just gamble on the slides?`,
                    coach_r4_starved:       `<strong>The exercise was electric — and then you spent 90 seconds on it.</strong> Under five minutes of debrief is how most of your learning just evaporated. The debrief is the lesson, not the afterthought.`,
                    coach_r4_plan_observed: `<strong>That measurement holds up.</strong> Observing behaviour on the job against the 58→70 rubric is what convinces a skeptical CLO that capability transferred. The guarantee is defensible.`,
                    coach_r4_plan_happy:    `<strong>A happy sheet measures the wrong thing.</strong> 20% of the fee rides on capability at work in 60 days, not on how today felt. What will you actually observe, and who observes it?`,
                    coach_r4_cutdebrief:    `<strong>You cut the debrief to protect the exercise.</strong> That's the most common and most costly design error — you protected the experience and sacrificed the learning it was for.`,

                    sum_default:            `Design move made.`,
